-- Step 41: payroll runs, their payslips, and the commission they carry.
-- track: C
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/payroll-runs/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by
-- Drizzle. Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A month's run is worked out by the app as a draft (one payslip for each person employed in the
-- month, from Step 40's pay, attendance and statutory tables, and the commission approved for
-- them), reviewed by the owner or the payroll administrator, approved by the owner or an
-- accountant, and paid out of a cash or bank account. Before approval it is worked out again or
-- cancelled; after, it stands. Approval puts it in the books and settles the commission it
-- carries: commission was expensed when it was earned (drizzle/0027_commission_ledger.sql), so
-- approval moves it from Commission payable to Salaries payable and never expenses it again.
-- Approval is refused when anyone's commission has changed since the run was worked out.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE300 to SE399 (docs/PARALLEL.md):
--   SE350  someone's commission has changed since the run was worked out
--   SE351  the app writes only a draft: its payslips, and a draft or reviewed run worked out again
--   SE352  payroll is run in read committed transactions
--   SE353  no such payroll run in this company
--   SE354  the run is not at the stage this needs (review a draft, approve a reviewed run, ...)
--   SE355  a date the run cannot have: a month not yet begun, a payment before approval
--   SE356  the run does not add up, or is out of date: work it out again
--   SE357  something is being recorded on one of the person's invoices right now; try again
--   SE358  commission is settled on or after the day it was released
--   SE359  salaries are paid from a cash or bank account that is in use

-- ── generated by drizzle-kit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

